{{!-- FusionSpace HPR's additions to every page's head (#383; `web.md`, *Using it in a project*
     and *Theme*): the page draws in light and dark, and the browser's own bar takes Paper on a
     light system and Void on a dark one, as the product system's `kit/web/head.html` sets them.
     mdBook puts this before its own `theme-color` of white, so a browser takes these first.
     `cargo xtask site` checks every built page for both. --}}
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#F3F4F7" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0B0F1C" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
{{!-- The four faces a page's first screen draws in, asked for as the head is read rather than
     once the stylesheet has arrived and named them: body text (Archivo), titles (Cascadia Mono
     SemiBold), inline code (Cascadia Mono) and bold text (Archivo SemiBold). A face that arrives
     after the text is drawn redraws it in other widths, which moved whole paragraphs on a phone
     (#443's CLS; ADR-232). The build asks for the stylesheet and mdBook's sidebar script just
     before these, as the page can't be drawn without them (`xtask/src/site/bundle.rs`). --}}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ path_to_root }}fonts/Archivo-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="{{ path_to_root }}fonts/CascadiaMono-SemiBold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="{{ path_to_root }}fonts/CascadiaMono-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="{{ path_to_root }}fonts/Archivo-SemiBold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
